  "description": "Stout, resilient mountain-dwellers. Family names and clan names are central to their identity.",
  "lore": "Dwarven names are typically harsh-sounding, with lots of consonants, umlauts, and 'kh' sounds — a legacy of their Duergar and Norse-inspired linguistic roots. A dwarf is usually known by their clan name (the 'patronym') which precedes the given name: 'Balin son of Fundal' or 'Thorgrim Ironbeard'. Dwarves of the same clan share the clan name. Female dwarf names often rhyme or have softer endings, but are no less fierce-sounding than the men's.",
